{"id": "EUVD-2026-101564", "enisaUuid": "546432ba-28a7-3c12-ace9-bdab19ca0090", "description": "AstronRPA through 1.1.6 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability in the resource-service /file/download endpoint that allows authenticated users to download other tenants' files by supplying their fileId. Attackers can enumerate predictable time-ordered Snowflake file IDs, since FileMapper.getFile performs no owner or tenant check, to retrieve S3-stored files uploaded by other tenants.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T18:47:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T14:35:55", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/iflytek-astron-rpa-file-download-cross-tenant-idor", "https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa/blob/b66e7c9e445906583c161bc9925432d6d39ca001/backend/resource-service/src/main/java/com/iflytek/rpa/resource/file/dao/FileMapper.java#L18", "https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/astronrpa-through-1.1.6-cross-tenant-file-disclosure-via-file-download"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110764", "GHSA-xg73-6f4x-27x7"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "489edd1d-dede-3061-8e70-8f4256ebb05e", "product": {"name": "astron-rpa", "vendor": {"name": "iflytek"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.1.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "85657675-7a1f-35d2-bcc1-4c1f990786b8", "vendor": {"name": "iflytek"}}], "isExploited": false}